                        "CanStart": true,
                        "ReframedTask": "### Reframed Task Description:\n\n#### Task Intent:\nDetermine the percentage of the United States (US) GDP that is contributed by New York state in the year 2024. This helps understand New York\u0027s economic significance in the national economy.\n\n#### Prerequisite Information:\n1. **New York State GDP for 2024**: The GDP for New York state is estimated to be **$2,200,000 million (or $2.2 trillion)**.\n2. **US GDP for 2024**: The GDP for the United States is estimated to be **$28.5 trillion**.\n\n#### Instructions:\n1. Use the GDP figures provided for New York state and the United States for the year 2024.\n2. Calculate the percentage of the US GDP that New York state\u0027s GDP represents. Perform the calculation using the following formula:  \n   \\[\n   \\text{Percentage Contribution} = \\left(\\frac{\\text{New York State GDP}}{\\text{US GDP}}\\right) \\times 100\n   \\]\n3. Ensure the result is expressed as a percentage rounded to two decimal places for clarity.\n\n#### Example Calculation:\nGiven:\n- New York state GDP: **$2,200,000 million**\n- US GDP: **$28,500,000 million**\n\nPerform:\n\\[\n\\text{Percentage Contribution} = \\left(\\frac{2,200,000}{28,500,000}\\right) \\times 100\n\\]\n\n#### Expected Output:\nProvide the percentage contributed by New York state\u0027s GDP relative to the US GDP for 2024, as well as any additional insights obtained from the calculation (e.g., relative significance of New York\u0027s economy in the national context).\n\n"
